quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  29,7,"As for those who believe and perform righteous deeds, We shall most surely absolve them of their misdeeds. And We shall most certainly reward them the best of what they used to do."
  29,8,"And We have commanded human being to be good to his parents. But if they urge you to associate with Me what you have no knowledge of, then do not obey them. To Me will be your return, and I will inform you of what you used to do."
  29,9,"And those who believe and perform righteous deeds, We shall surely admit them into (the company of) the virtuous."
  29,10,"There are some among the people who say: ‘We believe in Allah.’ But if such a person is made to suffer in Allah’s cause, he takes the persecution by the people as Allah’s punishment. Yet, if some help comes from your Lord, they will surely say: ‘We were indeed with you.’ Does not Allah know best what is (hidden) in the breasts of all creatures?"
  29,11,"Allah shall indeed distinguish those who have (truly) believed, and He will certainly expose the hypocrites."
  29,12,"And those who disbelieve say to the believers: ‘Follow our path, and we shall bear (the burden of) your wrongs.’ Yet they will never be the bearers of any of their wrongs. Indeed, they are liars."
  29,13,"But most surely, they shall carry their burdens and (many) other burdens along with their burdens. And they will indeed be questioned on the Day of Resurrection concerning what they used to fabricate."
  29,14,"Indeed, We sent Nuh (Noah) to his people. And he stayed among them for a thousand years, less fifty. Then, the flood overtook them while they were wrongdoers."
